---
source: packages/tier2/measure/tests/reliability.rs
expression: all
---
error[Z0401]: `reliability` needs at least two items, but `items:` names one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:33
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1])
  |                                 ^^^^^^ too few items
  |
  = help: a scale is the sum of several items: write them as a list, `[q1, q2, q3]` or `[q1..q3]`

error[Z0219]: `[]` alone has no type
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:33
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([])
  |                                 ^^ an empty list of what?
  |
  = help: where a parameter takes the list, its type is known; elsewhere give one value

error[Z0401]: `eng1` is written twice among the items of `reliability`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:33
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2, eng1])
  |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an item twice
  |
  = help: an item counted twice agrees with itself and raises alpha: name each item once

error[Z0101]: no variable `eng9` in `engagement`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:33
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng9])
  |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a variable of engagement
  |
  = help: did you mean `eng1`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"eng1"`

error[Z0401]: an item of `reliability` is a number or a Bool, but `industry` is a Category
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:28
  |
1 | dataset(wages).reliability([wage, industry])
  |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a number
  |
  = help: score the answers as numbers first, for example with `case` or `to(x, Int)`

error[Z0401]: `reverse:` names `eng4`, which is not among the items
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:56
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2], reverse: [eng4])
  |                                                        ^^^^^^ not an item
  |
  = help: `reverse:` lists the items of `items:` that are worded the other way round

note: 2 rows with NA in a or b dropped (line 1)
error[Z0401]: `reliability` needs at least two rows with every item, but there is one
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:51
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, NA, 3], b = [NA, 2, 4]).reliability([a, b])
  |                                                   ^^^^^^ too few rows
  |
  = help: a row with `NA` in any item is left out; check the items and the rows kept

error[Z0401]: the sum of the items is the same in every row, so `reliability` has no variation of the scale to divide by
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:55
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 2, 3, 4], b = [4, 3, 2, 1]).reliability([a, b])
  |                                                       ^^^^^^ a scale that does not vary
  |
  = help: check the items and the rows kept; items that cancel one another exactly may need `reverse:`

error[Z0401]: `c` has the same value in every row kept, so it cannot be standardized
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:97
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 2, 3, 4], b = [2, 1, 4, 3], c = [5, 5, 5, 5]).reliability([a, b, c], standardize: true)
  |                                                                                                 ^^^^ an item that does not vary
  |
  = help: leave the item out, or leave out `standardize: true`

error[Z0803]: `a` has values too large to compute with (above 1e150 in size)
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:59
  |
1 | frame(a = [1e200, 2, 3, 4], b = [2, 1, 4, 3]).reliability([a, b])
  |                                                           ^^^^^^ a variable too large to square
  |
  = help: divide the variable by a power of ten first, `add(a_m = a / 1e6)`, and read the result in those units; no p-value changes

error[Z0401]: `level:` of `reliability` is a confidence level between 0 and 1, but this is 1.5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:54
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2], level: 1.5)
  |                                                      ^^^ outside (0, 1)
  |
  = help: write a level such as 0.95 or 0.99

error[Z0402]: `bootstrap` is not one of the allowed words
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:51
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2], ci: bootstrap)
  |                                                   ^^^^^^^^^ expected one of feldt, duhachek

error[Z0401]: `standardize` of `reliability` must be a Bool, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:60
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2], standardize: 1)
  |                                                            ^ an Int
  |
  = help: usage: `data.reliability(items, standardize: Bool = false, reverse: Vars, ci: feldt | duhachek = feldt, level: Float = 0.95)`

error[Z0406]: `reliability` needs `items`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:21
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability()
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^ `items` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.reliability(items, standardize: Bool = false, reverse: Vars, ci: feldt | duhachek = feldt, level: Float = 0.95)`

error[Z0404]: `reliability` has no argument called `omega`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:47
  |
1 | dataset(engagement).reliability([eng1, eng2], omega: true)
  |                                               ^^^^^ unknown argument
